# A dynamic call of a `&&self` method consumes its trait value (a
# binding, a temporary, a struct field, an element popped off a list): the
# box hands its payload to the implementation, which ends it once, and the
# box is freed, so millions of such calls keep the resident set flat.
fixture: trait_values_free_at_their_last_owner_when_a_move_method_consumes_them.fixture
env: NO_COLOR=1
step: jet run -O0 main.jet
limit: time=120
exit: 0
stdout: = trait_values_free_at_their_last_owner_when_a_move_method_consumes_them.out
step: jet run -O1 main.jet
limit: time=120
exit: 0
stdout: = trait_values_free_at_their_last_owner_when_a_move_method_consumes_them.out
step: jet run -O2 main.jet
limit: time=120
exit: 0
stdout: = trait_values_free_at_their_last_owner_when_a_move_method_consumes_them.out
step: jet build main.jet
exit: 0
step aot: built
limit: time=120
exit: 0
stdout: = trait_values_free_at_their_last_owner_when_a_move_method_consumes_them.out
